{"assets":[],"contentKind":"statement","contestId":"2002","diagnostics":[],"document":{"children":[{"attrs":{"level":1,"role":"title"},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"F1. Court Blue (Easy Version)"}],"kind":"heading"},{"attrs":{"role":"time_limit"},"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"time limit per test"},{"kind":"text","text":":"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":"3 seconds"}],"kind":"container"},{"attrs":{"role":"memory_limit"},"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"memory limit per test"},{"kind":"text","text":":"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":"512 megabytes"}],"kind":"container"},{"attrs":{"role":"body"},"children":[{"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"This is the easy version of the problem. In this version, $$$n=m$$$ and the time limit is lower. You can make hacks only if both versions of the problem are solved."}],"kind":"container"}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"In the court of the Blue King, Lelle and Flamm are having a performance match. The match consists of several rounds. In each round, either Lelle or Flamm wins."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Let $$$W_L$$$ and $$$W_F$$$ denote the number of wins of Lelle and Flamm, respectively. The Blue King considers a match to be "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"successful"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":" if and only if:"}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"attrs":{"ordered":false},"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":" after every round, $$$\\gcd(W_L,W_F)\\le 1$$$; "}],"kind":"list_item"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":" at the end of the match, $$$W_L\\le n, W_F\\le m$$$. "}],"kind":"list_item"}],"kind":"list"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Note that $$$\\gcd(0,x)=\\gcd(x,0)=x$$$ for every non-negative integer $$$x$$$."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Lelle and Flamm can decide to stop the match whenever they want, and the final score of the performance is $$$l \\cdot W_L + f \\cdot W_F$$$."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Please help Lelle and Flamm coordinate their wins and losses such that the performance is "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"successful"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":", and the total score of the performance is maximized."}],"kind":"paragraph"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"input_specification"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":2},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Input"}],"kind":"heading"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"The first line contains an integer $$$t$$$ ($$$1\\leq t \\leq 10^3$$$) — the number of test cases."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"The only line of each test case contains four integers $$$n$$$, $$$m$$$, $$$l$$$, $$$f$$$ ($$$2\\leq n\\leq m \\leq 2\\cdot 10^7$$$, $$$1\\leq l,f \\leq 10^9$$$, $$$\\bf{n=m}$$$): $$$n$$$, $$$m$$$ gives the upper bound on the number of Lelle and Flamm's wins, $$$l$$$ and $$$f$$$ determine the final score of the performance."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Unusual additional constraint"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":": it is guaranteed that, for each test, there are no pairs of test cases with the same pair of $$$n$$$, $$$m$$$."}],"kind":"paragraph"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"output_specification"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":2},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Output"}],"kind":"heading"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"For each test case, output a single integer — the maximum total score of a "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"successful"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":" performance."}],"kind":"paragraph"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"samples"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":2},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Examples"}],"kind":"heading"},{"attrs":{"role":"sample"},"children":[{"attrs":{"role":"sample_input"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":3},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Input"}],"kind":"heading"},{"kind":"code_block","text":"\n8\n3 3 2 5\n4 4 1 4\n6 6 2 2\n7 7 2 3\n9 9 9 1\n2 2 1 4\n5 5 1 4\n8 8 6 7\n"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"sample_output"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":3},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Output"}],"kind":"heading"},{"kind":"code_block","text":"\n19\n17\n18\n33\n86\n9\n24\n86\n"}],"kind":"section"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"sample"},"children":[{"attrs":{"role":"sample_input"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":3},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Input"}],"kind":"heading"},{"kind":"code_block","text":"\n1\n20000000 20000000 1341 331\n"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"sample_output"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":3},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Output"}],"kind":"heading"},{"kind":"code_block","text":"\n33439999007\n"}],"kind":"section"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"sample"},"children":[{"attrs":{"role":"sample_input"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":3},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Input"}],"kind":"heading"},{"kind":"code_block","text":"\n2\n1984 1984 19 84\n9982 9982 44 35\n"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"sample_output"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":3},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Output"}],"kind":"heading"},{"kind":"code_block","text":"\n204143\n788403\n"}],"kind":"section"}],"kind":"section"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"note"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":2},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Note"}],"kind":"heading"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"In the first test case, a possible performance is as follows:"}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"attrs":{"ordered":false},"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":" Flamm wins, $$$\\gcd(0,1)=1$$$. "}],"kind":"list_item"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":" Lelle wins, $$$\\gcd(1,1)=1$$$. "}],"kind":"list_item"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":" Flamm wins, $$$\\gcd(1,2)=1$$$. "}],"kind":"list_item"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":" Flamm wins, $$$\\gcd(1,3)=1$$$. "}],"kind":"list_item"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":" Lelle wins, $$$\\gcd(2,3)=1$$$. "}],"kind":"list_item"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":" Lelle and Flamm agree to stop the match. "}],"kind":"list_item"}],"kind":"list"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"The final score is $$$2\\cdot2+3\\cdot5=19$$$."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"In the third test case, a possible performance is as follows:"}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"attrs":{"ordered":false},"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":" Flamm wins, $$$\\gcd(0,1)=1$$$. "}],"kind":"list_item"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":" Lelle wins, $$$\\gcd(1,1)=1$$$. "}],"kind":"list_item"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":" Lelle wins, $$$\\gcd(2,1)=1$$$. "}],"kind":"list_item"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":" Lelle wins, $$$\\gcd(3,1)=1$$$. "}],"kind":"list_item"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":" Lelle wins, $$$\\gcd(4,1)=1$$$. "}],"kind":"list_item"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":" Lelle wins, $$$\\gcd(5,1)=1$$$. "}],"kind":"list_item"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":" Flamm wins, $$$\\gcd(5,2)=1$$$. "}],"kind":"list_item"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":" Flamm wins, $$$\\gcd(5,3)=1$$$. "}],"kind":"list_item"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":" Flamm wins, $$$\\gcd(5,4)=1$$$. "}],"kind":"list_item"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":" Lelle and Flamm agree to stop the match. "}],"kind":"list_item"}],"kind":"list"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"The final score is $$$5\\cdot2+4\\cdot2=18$$$. Note that Lelle and Flamm can stop the match even if neither of them has $$$n$$$ wins."}],"kind":"paragraph"}],"kind":"section"}],"kind":"document"},"index":"F1","problemCode":"2002F1","schema":2,"sourceKind":"html","sourceUrl":"https://codeforces.com/contest/2002/problem/F1"}